  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the target of the meme's rhetorical accusation",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the text 'mandatory vaccinations \"no exemptions\"' as the intended recipient of the meme's message. The meme frames the user as someone who might be subject to or support such a policy, and thus is being warned or condemned by the visual association with Hitler. The projection is not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me' text), but is implied through the rhetorical structure: the user is positioned as the potential target of the policy being equated with totalitarianism. The user is projected onto the textual material as the subject of the meme's fear-based argument.",
